import EvmLogic.Chain.SystemCall
import EvmLogic.GasMono.CodeScan
import EvmLogic.Tx.Delete

/-!
# The canonical code of the system contracts

The four system contracts a block calls (`systemContracts`) hold fixed code, given by their EIPs
(EIP-4788, EIP-2935, EIP-7002, EIP-7251) and deployed on mainnet by the keyless transactions of
those EIPs. `systemCode a` is that runtime code at each system contract (empty elsewhere). The
bytes are those of `contracts/system/*.hex`: the code of the four accounts on Ethereum mainnet
(`eth_getCode` at block 26,270,327, October 2026), identical to their code in the pre-state of
the execution-spec-tests v5.4.0 Prague fixtures, with the code hashes returned by `eth_getProof`
noted on each constant.

None of them can act outside its own account (`isolated_systemCode`): no instruction of the
code (the linear decoding, `PUSH` immediates skipped: `GasMono.boundaries`) is a `CALL`,
`CALLCODE`, `DELEGATECALL`, `STATICCALL`, `CREATE`, `CREATE2`, `SELFDESTRUCT` or `GAS`
(`Isolated`), decided on the structural scan `GasMono.insns`. Each is real code: not empty and
not an EIP-7702 designator (`realCode_systemCode`).
-/

namespace EvmLogic.Chain
open EvmLean EvmLean.Interpreter EvmLean.Block EvmLogic.GasMono

